%N A398588 Decimal expansion of Re(Li_4((1 + i))/2), where Li_4(z) is the polylogarithm function of order 4, and i is the imaginary unit.
%H A398588 Narendra Bhandari, <a href="http://doi.org/10.7546/nntdm.2024.30.3.613-633">Evaluation of the real parts of polylogarithm expressions containing complex arguments via certain logarithmic integrals</a>, Notes on Number Theory and Discrete Mathematics, Vol. 30, No. 3 (2024), pp. 613-633. See Theorem 4.1, p. 628.
%H A398588 Seán Mark Stewart, <a href="https://doi.org/10.2478/tmmp-2020-0034">Explicit Evaluation of Some Quadratic Euler-Type Sums Containing Double-Index Harmonic Numbers</a>, Tatra Mountains Mathematical Publications, Vol. 77, No. 1 (2020), pp. 73-98; <a href="https://sciendo.com/pdf/10.2478/tmmp-2020-0034">alternative link</a>. See p. 95, eq. (45).
%H A398588 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.53, pp. 450-451, eq. (4.175) and (4.177), section 5.53, p. 468, section 6.53, pp. 770-779.
%H A398588 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Polylogarithm">Polylogarithm</a>.
%H A398588 Ming Hao Zhao, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.12155">On logarithmic integrals, harmonic sums and variations</a>, arXiv:1911.12155 [math.CA], 2019-2020. See Proposition 9, p. 36.
%F A398588 Equals Re(Li_4((1 - i)/2)).
%F A398588 Equals (-1/6) * Integral_{x=0..1} x*log(1-x)^3/(1 + x^2) dx.
%F A398588 Equals 343*zeta(4)/1024 - 5*log(2)^2*zeta(2)/128 + log(2)^4/96 + 5*Li_4(1/2)/16.
%e A398588 0.495781121821838778435919754508679334614844410968559...
%t A398588 RealDigits[Re[PolyLog[4, (1+I)/2]], 10, 120][[1]]
%t A398588 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398588 RealDigits[343*Zeta[4]/1024 - 5*Log[2]^2*Zeta[2]/128 + Log[2]^4/96 + 5*PolyLog[4, 1/2]/16, 10, 120][[1]]
%o A398588 (PARI) real(polylog(4, (1+I)/2))
%o A398588 (PARI) 343*zeta(4)/1024 - 5*log(2)^2*zeta(2)/128 + log(2)^4/96 + 5*polylog(4, 1/2)/16
